Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||10-04-2000||05:43 PM||||Hi,<BR>I'm going to be replacing my dogbone soon, I'm definately going with the poly style.  I really like the look of Chris West's on West Coast Fiero's site: <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Mounts/DogBone.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Mounts/DogBone.html</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dogbonea.gif"> <BR>Does it really have the chrome look to it is what I'm wandering? (since it says it is aluminum)  I assume the poly bushings are the same as other sources.  Can anyone attest to it's worthwhile?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Michael Schaefer<BR>p.s. I'm not worried about increased engine vibrations, I had a poly bone on my 85 GT and loved it. <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-04-2000||07:27 PM||||If it's aluminum you can always polish it and then coat it with clear wheel paint to keep it bright.||||reg||1
